# What never needs to reach the build context.
#
# This matters more than it looks. The landing zone under data/ is hundreds of
# parquet files; without this, every `docker build` ships them to the daemon
# before the first instruction runs, and every one of them invalidates the cache
# on the next ingest.

# Data. Generated by the pipeline, never an input to it.
data/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Local environments and caches.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Rendered research output; `make notebook` regenerates it.
docs/research.html

# Notebooks are a developer surface, not a runtime one.
notebooks/

# Tests, and the pytest bootstrap that goes with them.
tests/
conftest.py

# The monitoring stack runs as its own containers from their own images.
monitoring/

# Compose and container definitions are inputs to the daemon, not to the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Makefile

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
